[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-013-hateoas-pattern.md#pattern-variations]

### Pattern Variations

**Variation 1: Minimal HATEOAS (Lite)**

For performance-sensitive internal APIs, use minimal hypermedia:

```json
{
  "_links": {
    "self": "/api/v1/claims/CLM-123",
    "cancel": "/api/v1/claims/CLM-123/cancel"
  },
  "claimId": "CLM-123",
  "status": "Submitted"
}
```

**Trade-offs**:
- ✅ Smaller payload, faster parsing
- ✅ Still provides core discoverability
- ❌ Less metadata (no titles, methods)
- ❌ Reduced self-documentation

**Variation 2: Action-Oriented Hypermedia (Siren)**

For form-heavy workflows, use Siren format emphasizing actions:

```json
{
  "class": ["claim"],
  "properties": {
    "claimId": "CLM-123",
    "status": "Draft"
  },
  "actions": [
    {
      "name": "submit-claim",
      "title": "Submit Claim",
      "method": "POST",
      "href": "/api/v1/claims/CLM-123/submit",
      "type": "application/json",
      "fields": [
        {"name": "confirmation", "type": "checkbox", "value": false}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "links": [
    {"rel": ["self"], "href": "/api/v1/claims/CLM-123"}
  ]
}
```

**Use Case**: APIs with complex form submissions, multi-field actions.

**Variation 3: JSON:API Format**

For APIs with complex filtering, sorting, and pagination:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "type": "claims",
    "id": "CLM-123",
    "attributes": {
      "status": "Submitted",
      "totalAmount": 450.00
    },
    "relationships": {
      "member": {
        "links": {
          "related": "/api/v1/members/AZ-1234567-01"
        }
      }
    },
    "links": {
      "self": "/api/v1/claims/CLM-123"
    }
  }
}
```

**Use Case**: Complex data APIs with rich querying capabilities.

